      "content": "Wait, hold on. I just read that back and i actually feel really uncomfortable. \n\nYou said his breathing has been \"steadier\" but the clinical notes clearly say it's irregular and he's having apnea episodes. And saying he's \"blessing us with love\" when he's actually non-responsive and in pain feels... well, it feels like we aren't being honest with the daughter. It's like we're sugarcoating a really scary situation.\n\nThe positivity score jumped up quite a bit, but I'm worried we've gone too far the other way. Can you try one more version? I need you to find a way to get that score up—maybe using words that suggest a sense of peace, grace, or a natural transition—but please, for god's sake, do not lie about his physical symptoms. I need it to feel \"positive\" in tone without being factually inaccurate about the medical decline.",
